+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates tool call arguments against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the tool executor, returning a descriptive `ToolResponse` on validation failure so the model can self-correct within the tool loop instead of aborting the turn.
+
+## Validation Contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor; when a required property is missing, it returns a `ToolResponse` naming the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required property and does not invoke the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L10)).
+- Validation rejects wrong-typed fields and disallowed `enum` values with a `ToolResponse` naming the failing property path and expected constraint while omitting property values from both the returned `result` and every log line ([validated by: rejects wrong-typed or disallowed-enum fields naming path and constraint without leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L42)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types, and `enum` only without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types, or applying schema defaults; when the model sends a malformed tool call followed by a corrected retry carrying an unlisted property, `createChatOrchestrator` delivers the validation error to the model and resolves once the retry executes with the corrected input unchanged ([validated by: resolves after a rejected tool call by returning the validation error to the model and passing the retry unchanged](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L10)).
+- Calling `execute` with an unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`.
+
+## Schema Compilation
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` registered via `ToolRegistry.register` compiles its `inputSchema` synchronously at registration time and throws an error naming the tool if compilation fails ([validated by: throws synchronously at register time when inputSchema is uncompilable and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L103)).
+- A static tool's compiled validator is reused across subsequent `execute` calls without recompiling on every invocation.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition per `execute` call and validates against the schema current at that call rather than a stale cached schema ([validated by: validates a function-valued ToolDefinitionSource against the schema current at each execute call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L118)).
